    "created_at": "2026-11-16T19:13:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T19:13:42Z",
    "body": "Thank you again for this report. It is fixed in `main` by PR #2202.\n\nWith `useRadiusArcs` on, the post now splits a near-180-degree arc (for example a helix half-turn) into smaller arcs. Each R arc is checked after rounding, so that its radius can always reach its end point. The Fanuc and Doosan posts keep one native I/J/K arc when the block also writes rotary words.\n\nThe fix ships in the next release (v0.23.0). You can test it now with a build from `main`.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
